# E §3.1 The order of the checks (tally 2.1.2, issue #23): the items' own checks take "the moves, the fills, the defs,
# the bands and the asks, one sort at a time in that order". The def at line 11 is no id (LOAD-KEY); the move written
# after it, at line 15, refuses its `on` (LOAD-LITERAL), and prints, since moves are checked before defs.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "a source"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

def fee: money PLN = rate

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

move pay: transfers
  on 2026-01-10

ask q: fee
=== expect
refused: LOAD-LITERAL a date in a rule; make it a version (m.tally:16)
